T*
(ACME PETROCHEMICAL DEMO COMPLEX - UNIT 2300) Tj
T*
(STANDARD OPERATING MANUAL: CONCENTRATION & DECOMPOSITION SECTION) Tj
T*
(Document Code: OM-2300 | Revision: Z1 | Approved Operations Manual) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(SECTION 1: PROCESS DESCRIPTION & NORMAL OPERATING ENVELOPE) Tj
T*
(1.1 Preflash Concentration Section \(V-2301, P-2301A/B, X-2301\):) Tj
T*
(- Dilute 28 wt% CHP feed \(Stream S210, 42,500 kg/hr\) is concentrated under 35 mmHgA vacuum in Preflash Column V-2301 to produce 82 wt% CHP bottoms \(Stream S229, 14,500 kg/hr\).) Tj
T*
(- Safe Operating Limits for V-2301:) Tj
T*
(  * Sump Temperature: Normal 92.0 degC | High Alarm 98.0 degC | High-High Trip TAHH-0402 = 105.0 degC \(Interlock I-2301\)) Tj
T*
(  * Overhead Vacuum: Normal 35.0 mmHgA | High Alarm 55.0 mmHgA | High-High Trip PAHH-0401 = 75.0 mmHgA) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1.2 Decomposer Reactor Section \(D-2304, E-2307, P-2304A/B, D-2310\):) Tj
T*
(- Concentrated 82 wt% CHP \(Stream S229\) is cleaved into equimolar Phenol and Acetone in Decomposer Reactor D-2304 using 180 ppmw Sulfuric Acid catalyst \(Stream S310\).) Tj
T*
(- Because CHP cleavage is strongly exothermic \(-1580 kJ/kg\), D-2304 operates as a back-mixed loop reactor with a 12.7:1 recycle ratio \(Stream S379 = 185,000 kg/hr\) cooled through Shell & Tube Exchanger E-2307 \(4.85 Gcal/hr\) so residual unreacted CHP in D-2304 stays below 0.8 wt%.) Tj
T*
(- Safe Operating Limits for D-2304:) Tj
T*
(  * Reactor Temperature: Normal 82.0 degC | High Alarm TAH-1301 = 92.0 degC | SIL-2 Trip TXSHH-1301 = 115.0 degC \(Interlock I-2304\)) Tj
T*
(  * Reactor Pressure: Normal 1.8 kg/cm2g | High Alarm PAH-1301 = 3.2 kg/cm2g | SIL-2 Trip PAHH-1301 = 5.5 kg/cm2g | PSV-2304A/B Set = 11.0 kg/cm2g) Tj
T*
(  * Reactor Level \(LT-1301\): Normal 55.0% | Low-Low LSLL = 20.0% | High-High LSHH = 82.0%) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
