T*
(OM-2300 PAGE 2 OF 5 - SECTION 2: NORMAL STARTUP SEQUENCE \(COLD INVENTORY ESTABLISHMENT\)) Tj
T*
(Step 1: Verify Emergency Cumene Quench Drum is filled with >= 35 m3 chilled Cumene at 30 degC and SIL-2 valve XV-1309 passes readiness check.) Tj
T*
(Step 2: Fill Decomposer Reactor D-2304 and Cooler E-2307 loop to 55% level \(LT-1301\) with pre-mixed Phenol/Acetone product \(0% CHP\) and establish 185,000 kg/hr circulation via P-2304A \(verify FT-1304 > 150,000 kg/hr\).) Tj
T*
(Step 3: Establish tempered cooling water flow through E-2307 via TV-1302 and warm circulation loop to 75.0 degC.) Tj
T*
(Step 4: Open Sulfuric Acid Catalyst Valve XV-1305 to establish 180 ppmw H2SO4 baseline in D-2304 BEFORE introducing any CHP feed \(CRITICAL RULE: Never introduce CHP into D-2304 without active acid catalyst and circulation, or unreacted CHP will accumulate > 5 wt% and trigger thermal runaway upon subsequent acid contact\).) Tj
T*
(Step 5: Slowly ramp Concentrated CHP feed \(Stream S229 from P-2301A\) in 10% increments while monitoring D-2304 exotherm \(TIC-1302 = 82.0 degC\).) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
